    "https://snc.edu/news/pressrelease/reese-hired-career-services-st-norbert-college": {
      "title": "Reese hired in career services",
      "description": "Reese hired in career services at St. Norbert College | St. Norbert College Skip to main content Helpful info for Current students Parents & families Visitors Alumni Business & community Request info Apply Visit Give Popular Searches Events Careers Academic calendar Library Bookstore Academics Undergraduate programs Graduate programs Schneider Business School Faculty Statistics & outcomes Global experiences Support Admissions Visit Apply Tuition Why SNC? Resources Financial aid Aid application Financial aid types Tuition calculator Your offer Forms Scholarships Athletics About SNC Leadership Faculty Student life Mission & traditions Our values History & heritage Helpful info for Current students Parents & families Visitors Alumni Business & community Request Info Apply Now Visit SNC Give Today Academics Undergraduate programs Graduate programs Schneider Business School Faculty Statistics & outcomes Global experiences Support Admissions Visit Apply Tuition Why SNC? Resources Financial aid Aid application Financial aid types Tuition calculator Your offer Forms Scholarships Athletics About SNC Leadership Faculty Student life Mission & traditions Our values History & heritage Popular Searches Events Careers Academic calendar Library Bookstore PRESS RELEASE Reese hired in career services at St. Norbert College Posted on Aug. 7, 2007 Jenny Lee Reese, a native of Shiocton, Wis., joined the St. Norbert College career services department as an assistant director of internships and a career counselor in July. Reese earned her M.A. degree in counseling and student personnel from the University of Minnesota-Twin Cities in May 2007 after graduating from Ripon College in 2005 summa cum laude with a B.A. degree in business administration and sociology/anthropology. Before arriving at St. Norbert College, Reese interned at the Career and Community Learning Center for the College of Liberal Arts at the University of Minnesota-Twin Cities. She also participated in Federal TRIO programs, including Student Support Services, which work to retain college-level students, and Upward Bound, designed to aid high school students in their transition to college. According to Reese, these educational programs motivate and support students from disadvantaged backgrounds, including first generation students who may have disabilities or come from low-income families. In addition to her work with these programs, Reese co-instructed a career and major exploration class and assisted in the instruction of sociology courses at her alma mater, the University of Minnesota-Twin Cities. Contact info News & Events St. Norbert College 920-403-3048 communications@snc.edu Submit an Idea Media Inquiries Related News Press release St. Norbert College among 2026-2027… Read the article Press release New transfer agreement creates… Read the article Press release St. Norbert College ranks in top… Read the article Loading... Request info Apply Visit Give Apply Now Location 100 Grant Street De Pere, WI 54115 Visit Popular links News Events mySNC Bookstore Next steps Request info Apply Visit Give TITLE IX NON-DISCRIMINATION HUMAN RESOURCES PRIVACY STATEMENT CONTACT US SITE ACCESSIBILITY"
    }
  },
